                                                <msName>Pentateuch, for Samaritan use</msName>
                                            </msIdentifier>
                                            <msContents>
                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Pentateuch, for Samaritan use</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-1">
                                                    <locus from="3v" to="3v"/>
                                                    <title>Introduction of Abū Saʿīd</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-2">
                                                    <locus from="4v" to="120"/>
                                                    <title>Genesis</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <incipit>
                                                        <quote xml:lang="ar">البداية خلق الله السموات و الارض و الارض كانت مغمورة و مستبحرة وظلاما على وجه الغمر</quote>
                                                    </incipit>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-3">
                                                    <locus from="120v" to="218"/>
                                                    <title>Exodus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-4">
                                                    <locus from="218v" to="276"/>
                                                    <title>Leviticus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-5">
                                                    <locus from="276v" to="365v"/>
                                                    <title>Numbers</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-6">
                                                    <locus from="366" to="444"/>
                                                    <title>Deuteronomy</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-3-item-7">
                                                    <locus from="444v" to="475v"/>
                                                    <title>Glosses</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">A note at f. 446 states that the glosses are by Yūsuf ibn Abī Saʿīd and Ṣadaqa ibn Mīḫā.</note>
                                                </msItem>
                                            </msContents>
                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Western paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_7f4f7ddddf36c764710257): 13 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 150 × 85 mm., encadrée de filets rubriqués. Alphabets sémitiques (f. 1 v) ; invocations (f. 4) ; liste de 74 écritures (f. 477 v).Papier occidental.477 fol. (f. 477 laissé on blanc).Écriture orientale (Syrie). Premiers mots des chapitres en hébreu écrit en caractères samaritains.200 × 150 mm.Reliure du XVIIe s., peau chamoisée. Fleurons et filets estampés à chaud. Tranches bruinées.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">477 folios (f. 477 blank)</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">200</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">150</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">13 lines per page; written space framed by rubricated rules. The notice also records Semitic alphabets at f. 1v, invocations at f. 4, and a list of 74 scripts at f. 477v.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="13" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">150</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">85</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Syrian. First words of chapters are in Hebrew written in Samaritan characters.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <decoDesc>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Rubricated framing rules.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                </decoDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">17th-century chamois leather binding; fleurons and fillets stamped in gold; burnished edges.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_7f4f7ddddf36c764710257): Pentateuque, à l&apos;usage des Samaritains. Date described in the BnF catalogue: 1685.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Anonymous notice. Mentions of births and deaths at ff. 2v-3; reading marks at f. 2; act of sale of the copied manuscript at f. 3.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <acquisition>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Entered in 1860 from the Bibliothèque Sainte-Geneviève.</note>
                                                </acquisition>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" when="1685">1685</origDate>
                                                    <p>Copy made by Yūḥannā ibn Ǧirǧis ibn Qaṭā of Damascus and completed in Paris in 1685 (f. 475v).</p>
                                                    <p>A note states that the manuscript was copied from an old exemplar that had belonged to Yūsuf, a Samaritan physician of Damascus (f. 476). Another note says that this exemplar was brought to Marseille by the Capuchins and delivered to the scribe in Paris by Père Honoré d’Auxerre on 13 Tammūz 1684 (f. 476v).</p>
                                                </origin>
                                            </history>
